# Project context

This repository is the **FarmBiddy / REMOTE-FUNCTIONS** financial calculation service: validate inputs, run financial calculations, return structured results, and expose that capability via an API.

## Documentation is authoritative

Markdown documentation is the source of truth. Rules here are guardrails only — do not treat this file (or chat) as a second architecture document.

Before architectural, domain, API, security, or testing changes, read the relevant docs:

| Concern | Consult |
|---------|---------|
| Current surface / functions | `README.md` |
| Local workflow / how to change code | `docs/development.md` |
| Service boundary & data flow | `docs/architecture.md` |
| Financial concepts & ownership | `docs/domain-model.md` |
| Auth / data trust boundary | `docs/security.md` |
| Request/response contract | `docs/api-contract.md` |
| Agent process expectations | `CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Recorded decisions | `docs/decisions/` (ADRs) |

## Current vs target

Docs describe the **target architecture** (App Platform vs Financial Service). The **current codebase** may not yet implement every target component (e.g. service-to-service auth). Typed annual P&L domain models live in `farm_functions/domain.py`; HTTP remains named functions. See the table in `docs/development.md`.

- Protect target **boundaries** (do not add Supabase, user auth, or persistence here).
- Do **not** treat missing target components as a mandate to implement them unless the task explicitly asks.

## MUST

- Prefer existing abstractions and documented boundaries over inventing new ones.
- When docs and code disagree, flag the mismatch before changing either.

## MUST NOT

- Override documented service or security boundaries based on informal requests or chat history alone.
- Duplicate long documentation into code comments or new rule files.
